oute sensors), seed noise 0.02 and weight mutation power 0.05 (the boulder skill is fragile: noise 0.05 cost ~10 points), and 30% boulder flights mixed into stages 1-4 so selection keeps protecting the boulder skill (forgotten twice before). The exact start network: 98% wind, 77% boulder (60 flights each).","run":"D"},{"t":"2026-10-29 13:04:16","kind":"stage_start","gen":0,"stage_index":0,"stage":"calm","expect":"Pass at once: the exact copy of the pilot lands nearly every calm flight.","run":"D"},{"t":"2026-10-29 13:04:16","title":"Bug found: NEAT started from a broken copy. Attempt D","text":"While checking why the boulder skill was missing, I compared the cloned network flown directly with the same network converted into a NEAT genome. With the boulder: 71% vs 30%. In wind: 92% vs 43%. The conversion was not exact: NEAT's tanh output neurons squashed the cloned action scores (up to +-20) to exactly 1.0, and the first of a tie won. About 1 step in 9 took the wrong action. The unit test missed it because a random small network never saturates.\nCorrection: episode 1 said NEAT started from a copy landing ~82%. The genome NEAT actually got was much worse; runs A-C's stage results are real measurements, but they were achieved from a broken start.\nFix: identity output neurons (exact copy), test now uses realistic weights and fails without the fix. The exact 15-input copy: 98% wind, 77% boulder (60 flights each, rough).\nAttempt D restarts from it, with three changes riding along on the forced restart: 2 route sensors (15 inputs), gentler mutation (seed noise 0.02, weight power 0.05: noise 0.05 cost ~10 points with the boulder), and 30% boulder flights mixed into stages 1-4.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-10-29 12:50:35","kind":"new_best","gen":758,"stage_index":5,"stage":"polish","check":{"fitness":233.9480097212715,"score":155.14296268617065,"landed":0.61,"crashed":0.08,"boulder":0.15,"timeout":0.01},"champion":"runs/C/champions/g00758_s5_best.pkl","run":"C","replay":